-- title:
--   Regularity at cusp centres on the Gauss branch of X_H
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity and admitting a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((\mathsf q))$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H =$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, acting on $K$ compatibly, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating that maximal ideal. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of $\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ whose elements are exactly the $f$ for which there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((\mathsf q))$ after applying $A \to L$ coefficientwise (the Gauss valuation ring). Write $B$ for `chartAlgInf`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. The assertion is: for every prime ideal $y$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$, containing the element $j^{-1}$ of $B$, and containing every $b \in B$ whose image in $K$ lies in the nonunits of $W_0$, and for every commutative $B$-algebra $B_m$ that is a localisation of $B$ at $y$, the ring $B_m$ is a regular local ring and so is $B_m$ modulo the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the per-point form of the cusp-regularity statement for the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ along the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation ring: at every prime of the pole chart lying over $(\varpi)$, over $j = \infty$, and over the maximal ideal of $W_0$, both the local ring and its special fibre are regular. It feeds the regularity statement for primes of the two-chart model outside the image of the finite chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_xH_of_isAlgebraic.lean

